{"sha":"7bab09631c2a303f87a7eb7e3d69e888673b9b7e","node_id":"MDY6Q29tbWl0MjMyNTI5ODo3YmFiMDk2MzFjMmEzMDNmODdhN2ViN2UzZDY5ZTg4ODY3M2I5Yjdl","commit":{"author":{"name":"Vladis Dronov","email":"vdronov@redhat.com","date":"2017-08-02T17:50:14Z"},"committer":{"name":"Steffen Klassert","email":"steffen.klassert@secunet.com","date":"2017-08-03T08:15:22Z"},"message":"xfrm: policy: check policy direction value\n\nThe 'dir' parameter in xfrm_migrate() is a user-controlled byte which is used\nas an array index. This can lead to an out-of-bound access, kernel lockup and\nDoS. Add a check for the 'dir' value.\n\nThis fixes CVE-2017-11600.\n\nReferences: https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=1474928\nFixes: 80c9abaabf42 (\"[XFRM]: Extension for dynamic update of endpoint address(es)\")\nCc: <stable@vger.kernel.org> # v2.6.21-rc1\nReported-by: \"bo Zhang\" <zhangbo5891001@gmail.com>\nSigned-off-by: Vladis Dronov <vdronov@redhat.com>\nSigned-off-by: Steffen Klassert <steffen.klassert@secunet.com>","tree":{"sha":"ac79589b4b637637506f7989d8e2d06c4c2807ab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/torvalds/linux/git/trees/ac79589b4b637637506f7989d8e2d06c4c2807ab"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/torvalds/linux/git/commits/7bab09631c2a303f87a7eb7e3d69e888673b9b7e","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/torvalds/linux/commits/7bab09631c2a303f87a7eb7e3d69e888673b9b7e","html_url":"https://github.com/torvalds/linux/commit/7bab09631c2a303f87a7eb7e3d69e888673b9b7e","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/torvalds/linux/commits/7bab09631c2a303f87a7eb7e3d69e888673b9b7e/comments","author":{"login":"nefigtut","id":35604488,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1NjA0NDg4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35604488?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nefigtut","html_url":"https://github.com/nefigtut","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/user